{#
    `.. topic::` as the reStructuredText parser builds it — the spelling an
    author actually writes, and a different node from the one `body/topic`
    renders. Both are overridden because both are reachable, and a theme that
    covered one of them would look right until somebody wrote the other.

    Same shape, same reasoning: see `body/topic.html.twig` for why an `<aside>`
    on `.sds-panel` and not an admonition.

    The classes from the source come along. An author who wrote `:class:` on a
    topic meant it for their own stylesheet, and dropping it silently is the
    one thing a theme must not do with what it does not understand.
#}
<aside class="topic sds-panel{% if node.classes %} {{ node.classesString }}{% endif %}">
    <p class="topic-title">{{ renderNode(node.content) }}</p>
    {{ renderNode(node.value) }}
</aside>
